  "question": {
    "text": "Let the curve $z(1+i)+\\bar{z}(1-i)=4, z \\in \\mathrm{C}$, divide the region $|z-3| \\leq 1$ into two parts of areas $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$. Then $|\\alpha-\\beta|$ equals :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "1AOMQ",
      "text": "$1+\\frac{\\pi}{2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "pIfwb",
      "text": "$1+\\frac{\\pi}{3}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "w1Tgw",
      "text": "$1+\\frac{\\pi}{6}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "OdMOB",
      "text": "$1+\\frac{\\pi}{4}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/RUAQsiBdybpBmPHacna6Oazdcv5gD3NtmZxd7bzKQek.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\n\n\n\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\text { Let } z=x+i y \\\\\n& (x+i y)(1+i)+(x-i y)(1-i)=4 \\\\\n& x+i x+i y-y+x-i x-i y-y=4 \\\\\n& 2 x-2 y=4 \\\\\n& x-y=2 \\\\\n& |z-3| \\leq 1 \\\\\n& (x-3)^2+y^2 \\leq 1\n\\end{aligned}$\n\nArea of shaded region $=\\frac{\\pi \\cdot 1^2}{4}-\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 1 \\cdot 1=\\frac{\\pi}{4}-\\frac{1}{2}$\nArea of unshaded region inside the circle\n$=\\frac{3}{4} \\pi \\cdot 1^2+\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 1 \\cdot 1=\\frac{3 \\pi}{4}+\\frac{1}{2}$\n$\\therefore$ difference of area $=\\left(\\frac{3 \\pi}{4}+\\frac{1}{2}\\right)-\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)$\n$=\\frac{\\pi}{2}+1$",
    "image": null
  },
